 "brief": "# Orchestrator: cheap redundancy check at split time (Brett, Nov 7)\n\nEvery time the orchestrator takes a build request and splits it into steps, it runs a CHEAP redundancy check before registering it. Plain code, zero AI tokens, fast (<2 s).\n\n1. Check the new build and each of its steps against: builds store/orchestrator (all builds, any status), Plan Studio plans + blueprints, Shipped features/feature-ledger, open branches in /root/axf-builds (names + commit subjects), and the asset registry (ui-registry) for UI steps.\n2. Matching: normalized title/summary similarity, shared keywords/ids, same files/assets touched, superseded rounds (-r2, -fable). Thresholds in orchestrator settings.\n3. On a hit: don't block silently. Attach findings to the build (\"looks like X, Y\") with suggested action (reuse/extend existing, merge into, skip step, proceed). Default: proceed and flag; setting to hold for Brett. Phone alert (AmberX) when a likely duplicate is found, answerable in place.\n4. Results feed the Maintenance redundancy-scan report (shared finding format; coordinate with build maintenance-redundancy-scan if it has landed, else define the shared format here).\n5. Settings in place, from assets, no hard-coded styling. Tests with known duplicates from today's store (e.g. skins r2/r3/r4, shipped-features rounds, handoff-2 copies). Add to Shipped features.\n\nProgress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push.",
